{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This guide covers updating and managing search parameters during navigation using TanStack Router's Link components and programmatic navigation methods."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Prerequisites:"}]},{"type":"text","value":" "},{"type":"link","href":"./setup-basic-search-params.md","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Set Up Basic Search Parameters"}]},{"type":"text","value":" - Foundation concepts for reading and validating search params."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"quick-start","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Quick Start"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Configure navigation that updates search parameters while preserving existing state:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { Link, useNavigate } from '@tanstack/react-router'\n\n// Link with search parameter updates\n;<Link to=\"/search\" search={(prev) => ({ ...prev, query: 'new search' })}>\n  Search for \"new search\"\n</Link>\n\n// Programmatic navigation\nconst navigate = useNavigate()\nnavigate({\n  to: '/search',\n  search: (prev) => ({ ...prev, page: 1 }),\n})","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"navigation-methods","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Navigation Methods"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"using-link-components","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Using Link Components"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":4,"id":"basic-search-parameter-updates","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Basic Search Parameter Updates"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Replace all search parameters:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { Link } from '@tanstack/router'\n\nfunction SearchForm() {\n  return (\n    <div>\n      {/* Replace all search params */}\n      <Link to=\"/products\" search={{ category: 'electronics', page: 1 }}>\n        Electronics\n      </Link>\n\n      {/* Navigate to same route with new search */}\n      <Link search={{ sort: 'price-asc' }}>Sort by Price</Link>\n    </div>\n  )\n}","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"heading","depth":4,"id":"functional-search-parameter-updates","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Functional Search Parameter Updates"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Merge with existing search parameters:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { Link } from '@tanstack/react-router'\n\nfunction Pagination() {\n  return (\n    <div>\n      {/* Preserve existing search, update page */}\n      <Link search={(prev) => ({ ...prev, page: (prev.page || 1) + 1 })}>\n        Next Page\n      </Link>\n\n      {/* Toggle filter while keeping other params */}\n      <Link\n        search={(prev) => ({\n          ...prev,\n          inStock: !prev.inStock,\n        })}\n      >\n        Toggle In Stock\n      </Link>\n\n      {/* Remove a search parameter */}\n      <Link\n        search={(prev) => {\n          const { category, ...rest } = prev\n          return rest\n        }}\n      >\n        Clear Category Filter\n      </Link>\n    </div>\n  )\n}","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"heading","depth":4,"id":"preserving-all-search-parameters","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Preserving All Search Parameters"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"search={true}"},{"type":"text","value":" to keep all current search parameters when navigating:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { Link } from '@tanstack/react-router'\n\nfunction Navigation() {\n  return (\n    <nav>\n      {/* Keep all search params when changing routes */}\n      <Link to=\"/products\" search={true}>\n        View Products (Keep Filters)\n      </Link>\n\n      {/* Equivalent functional approach */}\n      <Link to=\"/products\" search={(prev) => prev}>\n        View Products (Functional)\n      </Link>\n    </nav>\n  )\n}","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"heading","depth":4,"id":"navigation-with-route-changes","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Navigation with Route Changes"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Navigate to different routes with search parameters:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { Link } from '@tanstack/react-router'\n\nfunction Navigation() {\n  return (\n    <nav>\n      {/* Navigate to different route with search */}\n      <Link to=\"/search\" search={{ query: 'laptops', category: 'electronics' }}>\n        Search Laptops\n      </Link>\n\n      {/* Inherit current search params to new route */}\n      <Link\n        to=\"/products\"\n        search={true} // Shorthand to carry over all search params\n      >\n        View Products\n      </Link>\n\n      {/* Transform search params for new route */}\n      <Link\n        to=\"/advanced-search\"\n        search={(prev) => ({\n          q: prev.query, // Rename parameter\n          filters: {\n            category: prev.category,\n            inStock: prev.inStock,\n          },\n        })}\n      >\n        Advanced Search\n      </Link>\n    </nav>\n  )\n}","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"programmatic-navigation","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Programmatic Navigation"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":4,"id":"using-usenavigate-hook","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Using useNavigate Hook"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Navigate programmatically with search parameter updates:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { useNavigate } from '@tanstack/react-router'\n\nfunction SearchControls() {\n  const navigate = useNavigate()\n\n  const handleSortChange = (sortBy: string) => {\n    navigate({\n      search: (prev) => ({ ...prev, sort: sortBy, page: 1 }),\n    })\n  }\n\n  const handleClearFilters = () => {\n    navigate({\n      search: (prev) => {\n        const { category, minPrice, maxPrice, ...rest } = prev\n        return rest\n      },\n    })\n  }\n\n  const handleSearch = (query: string) => {\n    navigate({\n      to: '/search',\n      search: { query, page: 1 },\n    })\n  }\n\n  return (\n    <div>\n      <select onChange={(e) => handleSortChange(e.target.value)}>\n        <option value=\"relevance\">Sort by Relevance</option>\n        <option value=\"price-asc\">Price: Low to High</option>\n        <option value=\"price-desc\">Price: High to Low</option>\n      </select>\n\n      <button onClick={handleClearFilters}>Clear Filters</button>\n\n      <button onClick={() => handleSearch('latest products')}>\n        Search Latest\n      </button>\n    </div>\n  )\n}","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"heading","depth":4,"id":"navigation-with-router-instance","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Navigation with Router Instance"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use the router directly only in non-React contexts where "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useNavigate"},{"type":"text","value":" or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Link"},{"type":"text","value":" aren't available:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { router } from './router' // Your router instance\n\n// ✅ Appropriate use case: Utility function outside React components\nexport function navigateFromUtility(searchParams: Record<string, any>) {\n  router.navigate({\n    search: (prev) => ({ ...prev, ...searchParams }),\n  })\n}\n\n// ✅ Appropriate use case: Event handlers in non-React code\nclass ApiService {\n  onAuthError() {\n    // Navigate to login when auth fails\n    router.navigate({\n      to: '/login',\n      search: { redirect: window.location.pathname },\n    })\n  }\n}\n\n// ✅ Appropriate use case: Global error handler\nwindow.addEventListener('unhandledrejection', (event) => {\n  if (event.reason.status === 401) {\n    router.navigate({\n      to: '/login',\n      search: { error: 'session-expired' },\n    })\n  }\n})","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"⚠️ In React components, prefer "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useNavigate"},{"type":"text","value":" instead:"}]}]},{"type":"code","value":"// ❌ Avoid in React components\nfunction Component() {\n  const router = useRouter()\n\n  const handleClick = () => {\n    router.navigate({ search: { filter: 'active' } })\n  }\n\n  return <button onClick={handleClick}>Filter</button>\n}\n\n// ✅ Use useNavigate in React components\nfunction Component() {\n  const navigate = useNavigate()\n\n  const handleClick = () => {\n    navigate({ search: { filter: 'active' } })\n  }\n\n  return <button onClick={handleClick}>Filter</button>\n}","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"advanced-navigation-patterns","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Advanced Navigation Patterns"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"conditional-navigation","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Conditional Navigation"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Navigate automatically when certain conditions are met:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { useEffect } from 'react'\nimport { useNavigate, useSearch } from '@tanstack/react-router'\n\nfunction ConditionalNavigation() {\n  const navigate = useNavigate()\n  const search = useSearch({ from: '/products' })\n\n  // Auto-reset page when search query changes\n  useEffect(() => {\n    if (search.query && search.page > 1) {\n      navigate({\n        search: (prev) => ({ ...prev, page: 1 }),\n      })\n    }\n  }, [search.query, search.page, navigate])\n\n  return <div>Page resets automatically when search changes</div>\n}","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"common-patterns","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Common Patterns"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"common-problems","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Common Problems"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"search-parameters-not-updating","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Search Parameters Not Updating"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Problem:"}]},{"type":"text","value":" Link navigation doesn't update search parameters."}]},{"type":"code","value":"// ❌ Wrong - no search prop\n<Link to=\"/products\">Electronics</Link>\n\n// ✅ Correct - with search parameters\n<Link to=\"/products\" search={{ category: 'electronics' }}>\n  Electronics\n</Link>","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"losing-existing-search-parameters","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Losing Existing Search Parameters"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Problem:"}]},{"type":"text","value":" New navigation replaces all search parameters instead of updating specific ones."}]},{"type":"code","value":"// ❌ Wrong - replaces all search params\n<Link search={{ page: 2 }}>Next Page</Link>\n\n// ✅ Correct - preserves existing search params\n<Link search={(prev) => ({ ...prev, page: 2 })}>\n  Next Page\n</Link>","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"common-next-steps","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Common Next Steps"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"After mastering navigation with search parameters, you might want to:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"./validate-search-params.md","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Validate Search Parameters with Schemas"}]},{"type":"text","value":" - Add robust validation with Zod, Valibot, or ArkType"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"./arrays-objects-dates-search-params.md","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Work with Arrays, Objects, and Dates"}]},{"type":"text","value":" - Handle arrays, objects, dates, and nested data structures"}]}]}]},{"type":"html","value":"<!-- Uncomment when guides are available\n- [Share Search Parameters Across Routes](./share-search-params-across-routes.md) - Inherit and manage search params across route hierarchies\n-->"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"related-resources","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Related Resources"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"https://tanstack.com/router/latest/docs/framework/react/guide/search-params","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TanStack Router Search Params Guide"}]},{"type":"text","value":" - Official documentation"}]}]}]}],"headings":[{"id":"quick-start","text":"Quick Start","level":2},{"id":"navigation-methods","text":"Navigation Methods","level":2},{"id":"using-link-components","text":"Using Link Components","level":3},{"id":"basic-search-parameter-updates","text":"Basic Search Parameter Updates","level":4},{"id":"functional-search-parameter-updates","text":"Functional Search Parameter Updates","level":4},{"id":"preserving-all-search-parameters","text":"Preserving All Search Parameters","level":4},{"id":"navigation-with-route-changes","text":"Navigation with Route Changes","level":4},{"id":"programmatic-navigation","text":"Programmatic Navigation","level":3},{"id":"using-usenavigate-hook","text":"Using useNavigate Hook","level":4},{"id":"navigation-with-router-instance","text":"Navigation with Router Instance","level":4},{"id":"advanced-navigation-patterns","text":"Advanced Navigation Patterns","level":2},{"id":"conditional-navigation","text":"Conditional Navigation","level":3},{"id":"common-patterns","text":"Common Patterns","level":2},{"id":"common-problems","text":"Common Problems","level":2},{"id":"search-parameters-not-updating","text":"Search Parameters Not Updating","level":3},{"id":"losing-existing-search-parameters","text":"Losing Existing Search Parameters","level":3},{"id":"common-next-steps","text":"Common Next Steps","level":2},{"id":"related-resources","text":"Related Resources","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\nThis guide covers updating and managing search parameters during navigation using TanStack Router's Link components and programmatic navigation methods.\n\n**Prerequisites:** [Set Up Basic Search Parameters](./setup-basic-search-params.md) - Foundation concepts for reading and validating search params.\n\n## Quick Start\n\nConfigure navigation that updates search parameters while preserving existing state:\n\n```tsx\nimport { Link, useNavigate } from '@tanstack/react-router'\n\n// Link with search parameter updates\n;<Link to=\"/search\" search={(prev) => ({ ...prev, query: 'new search' })}>\n  Search for \"new search\"\n</Link>\n\n// Programmatic navigation\nconst navigate = useNavigate()\nnavigate({\n  to: '/search',\n  search: (prev) => ({ ...prev, page: 1 }),\n})\n```\n\n## Navigation Methods\n\n### Using Link Components\n\n#### Basic Search Parameter Updates\n\nReplace all search parameters:\n\n```tsx\nimport { Link } from '@tanstack/router'\n\nfunction SearchForm() {\n  return (\n    <div>\n      {/* Replace all search params */}\n      <Link to=\"/products\" search={{ category: 'electronics', page: 1 }}>\n        Electronics\n      </Link>\n\n      {/* Navigate to same route with new search */}\n      <Link search={{ sort: 'price-asc' }}>Sort by Price</Link>\n    </div>\n  )\n}\n```\n\n#### Functional Search Parameter Updates\n\nMerge with existing search parameters:\n\n```tsx\nimport { Link } from '@tanstack/react-router'\n\nfunction Pagination() {\n  return (\n    <div>\n      {/* Preserve existing search, update page */}\n      <Link search={(prev) => ({ ...prev, page: (prev.page || 1) + 1 })}>\n        Next Page\n      </Link>\n\n      {/* Toggle filter while keeping other params */}\n      <Link\n        search={(prev) => ({\n          ...prev,\n          inStock: !prev.inStock,\n        })}\n      >\n        Toggle In Stock\n      </Link>\n\n      {/* Remove a search parameter */}\n      <Link\n        search={(prev) => {\n          const { category, ...rest } = prev\n          return rest\n        }}\n      >\n        Clear Category Filter\n      </Link>\n    </div>\n  )\n}\n```\n\n#### Preserving All Search Parameters\n\nUse `search={true}` to keep all current search parameters when navigating:\n\n```tsx\nimport { Link } from '@tanstack/react-router'\n\nfunction Navigation() {\n  return (\n    <nav>\n      {/* Keep all search params when changing routes */}\n      <Link to=\"/products\" search={true}>\n        View Products (Keep Filters)\n      </Link>\n\n      {/* Equivalent functional approach */}\n      <Link to=\"/products\" search={(prev) => prev}>\n        View Products (Functional)\n      </Link>\n    </nav>\n  )\n}\n```\n\n#### Navigation with Route Changes\n\nNavigate to different routes with search parameters:\n\n```tsx\nimport { Link } from '@tanstack/react-router'\n\nfunction Navigation() {\n  return (\n    <nav>\n      {/* Navigate to different route with search */}\n      <Link to=\"/search\" search={{ query: 'laptops', category: 'electronics' }}>\n        Search Laptops\n      </Link>\n\n      {/* Inherit current search params to new route */}\n      <Link\n        to=\"/products\"\n        search={true} // Shorthand to carry over all search params\n      >\n        View Products\n      </Link>\n\n      {/* Transform search params for new route */}\n      <Link\n        to=\"/advanced-search\"\n        search={(prev) => ({\n          q: prev.query, // Rename parameter\n          filters: {\n            category: prev.category,\n            inStock: prev.inStock,\n          },\n        })}\n      >\n        Advanced Search\n      </Link>\n    </nav>\n  )\n}\n```\n\n### Programmatic Navigation\n\n#### Using useNavigate Hook\n\nNavigate programmatically with search parameter updates:\n\n```tsx\nimport { useNavigate } from '@tanstack/react-router'\n\nfunction SearchControls() {\n  const navigate = useNavigate()\n\n  const handleSortChange = (sortBy: string) => {\n    navigate({\n      search: (prev) => ({ ...prev, sort: sortBy, page: 1 }),\n    })\n  }\n\n  const handleClearFilters = () => {\n    navigate({\n      search: (prev) => {\n        const { category, minPrice, maxPrice, ...rest } = prev\n        return rest\n      },\n    })\n  }\n\n  const handleSearch = (query: string) => {\n    navigate({\n      to: '/search',\n      search: { query, page: 1 },\n    })\n  }\n\n  return (\n    <div>\n      <select onChange={(e) => handleSortChange(e.target.value)}>\n        <option value=\"relevance\">Sort by Relevance</option>\n        <option value=\"price-asc\">Price: Low to High</option>\n        <option value=\"price-desc\">Price: High to Low</option>\n      </select>\n\n      <button onClick={handleClearFilters}>Clear Filters</button>\n\n      <button onClick={() => handleSearch('latest products')}>\n        Search Latest\n      </button>\n    </div>\n  )\n}\n```\n\n#### Navigation with Router Instance\n\nUse the router directly only in non-React contexts where `useNavigate` or `Link` aren't available:\n\n```tsx\nimport { router } from './router' // Your router instance\n\n// ✅ Appropriate use case: Utility function outside React components\nexport function navigateFromUtility(searchParams: Record<string, any>) {\n  router.navigate({\n    search: (prev) => ({ ...prev, ...searchParams }),\n  })\n}\n\n// ✅ Appropriate use case: Event handlers in non-React code\nclass ApiService {\n  onAuthError() {\n    // Navigate to login when auth fails\n    router.navigate({\n      to: '/login',\n      search: { redirect: window.location.pathname },\n    })\n  }\n}\n\n// ✅ Appropriate use case: Global error handler\nwindow.addEventListener('unhandledrejection', (event) => {\n  if (event.reason.status === 401) {\n    router.navigate({\n      to: '/login',\n      search: { error: 'session-expired' },\n    })\n  }\n})\n```\n\n**⚠️ In React components, prefer `useNavigate` instead:**\n\n```tsx\n// ❌ Avoid in React components\nfunction Component() {\n  const router = useRouter()\n\n  const handleClick = () => {\n    router.navigate({ search: { filter: 'active' } })\n  }\n\n  return <button onClick={handleClick}>Filter</button>\n}\n\n// ✅ Use useNavigate in React components\nfunction Component() {\n  const navigate = useNavigate()\n\n  const handleClick = () => {\n    navigate({ search: { filter: 'active' } })\n  }\n\n  return <button onClick={handleClick}>Filter</button>\n}\n```\n\n## Advanced Navigation Patterns\n\n### Conditional Navigation\n\nNavigate automatically when certain conditions are met:\n\n```tsx\nimport { useEffect } from 'react'\nimport { useNavigate, useSearch } from '@tanstack/react-router'\n\nfunction ConditionalNavigation() {\n  const navigate = useNavigate()\n  const search = useSearch({ from: '/products' })\n\n  // Auto-reset page when search query changes\n  useEffect(() => {\n    if (search.query && search.page > 1) {\n      navigate({\n        search: (prev) => ({ ...prev, page: 1 }),\n      })\n    }\n  }, [search.query, search.page, navigate])\n\n  return <div>Page resets automatically when search changes</div>\n}\n```\n\n## Common Patterns\n\n## Common Problems\n\n### Search Parameters Not Updating\n\n**Problem:** Link navigation doesn't update search parameters.\n\n```tsx\n// ❌ Wrong - no search prop\n<Link to=\"/products\">Electronics</Link>\n\n// ✅ Correct - with search parameters\n<Link to=\"/products\" search={{ category: 'electronics' }}>\n  Electronics\n</Link>\n```\n\n### Losing Existing Search Parameters\n\n**Problem:** New navigation replaces all search parameters instead of updating specific ones.\n\n```tsx\n// ❌ Wrong - replaces all search params\n<Link search={{ page: 2 }}>Next Page</Link>\n\n// ✅ Correct - preserves existing search params\n<Link search={(prev) => ({ ...prev, page: 2 })}>\n  Next Page\n</Link>\n```\n\n## Common Next Steps\n\nAfter mastering navigation with search parameters, you might want to:\n\n- [Validate Search Parameters with Schemas](./validate-search-params.md) - Add robust validation with Zod, Valibot, or ArkType\n- [Work with Arrays, Objects, and Dates](./arrays-objects-dates-search-params.md) - Handle arrays, objects, dates, and nested data structures\n\n<!-- Uncomment when guides are available\n- [Share Search Parameters Across Routes](./share-search-params-across-routes.md) - Inherit and manage search params across route hierarchies\n-->\n\n## Related Resources\n\n- [TanStack Router Search Params Guide](https://tanstack.com/router/latest/docs/framework/react/guide/search-params) - Official documentation\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\ntitle: How to Navigate with Search Parameters\n---\n\nThis guide covers updating and managing search parameters during navigation using TanStack Router's Link components and programmatic navigation methods.\n\n**Prerequisites:** [Set Up Basic Search Parameters](./setup-basic-search-params.md) - Foundation concepts for reading and validating search params.\n\n## Quick Start\n\nConfigure navigation that updates search parameters while preserving existing state:\n\n```tsx\nimport { Link, useNavigate } from '@tanstack/react-router'\n\n// Link with search parameter updates\n;<Link to=\"/search\" search={(prev) => ({ ...prev, query: 'new search' })}>\n  Search for \"new search\"\n</Link>\n\n// Programmatic navigation\nconst navigate = useNavigate()\nnavigate({\n  to: '/search',\n  search: (prev) => ({ ...prev, page: 1 }),\n})\n```\n\n## Navigation Methods\n\n### Using Link Components\n\n#### Basic Search Parameter Updates\n\nReplace all search parameters:\n\n```tsx\nimport { Link } from '@tanstack/router'\n\nfunction SearchForm() {\n  return (\n    <div>\n      {/* Replace all search params */}\n      <Link to=\"/products\" search={{ category: 'electronics', page: 1 }}>\n        Electronics\n      </Link>\n\n      {/* Navigate to same route with new search */}\n      <Link search={{ sort: 'price-asc' }}>Sort by Price</Link>\n    </div>\n  )\n}\n```\n\n#### Functional Search Parameter Updates\n\nMerge with existing search parameters:\n\n```tsx\nimport { Link } from '@tanstack/react-router'\n\nfunction Pagination() {\n  return (\n    <div>\n      {/* Preserve existing search, update page */}\n      <Link search={(prev) => ({ ...prev, page: (prev.page || 1) + 1 })}>\n        Next Page\n      </Link>\n\n      {/* Toggle filter while keeping other params */}\n      <Link\n        search={(prev) => ({\n          ...prev,\n          inStock: !prev.inStock,\n        })}\n      >\n        Toggle In Stock\n      </Link>\n\n      {/* Remove a search parameter */}\n      <Link\n        search={(prev) => {\n          const { category, ...rest } = prev\n          return rest\n        }}\n      >\n        Clear Category Filter\n      </Link>\n    </div>\n  )\n}\n```\n\n#### Preserving All Search Parameters\n\nUse `search={true}` to keep all current search parameters when navigating:\n\n```tsx\nimport { Link } from '@tanstack/react-router'\n\nfunction Navigation() {\n  return (\n    <nav>\n      {/* Keep all search params when changing routes */}\n      <Link to=\"/products\" search={true}>\n        View Products (Keep Filters)\n      </Link>\n\n      {/* Equivalent functional approach */}\n      <Link to=\"/products\" search={(prev) => prev}>\n        View Products (Functional)\n      </Link>\n    </nav>\n  )\n}\n```\n\n#### Navigation with Route Changes\n\nNavigate to different routes with search parameters:\n\n```tsx\nimport { Link } from '@tanstack/react-router'\n\nfunction Navigation() {\n  return (\n    <nav>\n      {/* Navigate to different route with search */}\n      <Link to=\"/search\" search={{ query: 'laptops', category: 'electronics' }}>\n        Search Laptops\n      </Link>\n\n      {/* Inherit current search params to new route */}\n      <Link\n        to=\"/products\"\n        search={true} // Shorthand to carry over all search params\n      >\n        View Products\n      </Link>\n\n      {/* Transform search params for new route */}\n      <Link\n        to=\"/advanced-search\"\n        search={(prev) => ({\n          q: prev.query, // Rename parameter\n          filters: {\n            category: prev.category,\n            inStock: prev.inStock,\n          },\n        })}\n      >\n        Advanced Search\n      </Link>\n    </nav>\n  )\n}\n```\n\n### Programmatic Navigation\n\n#### Using useNavigate Hook\n\nNavigate programmatically with search parameter updates:\n\n```tsx\nimport { useNavigate } from '@tanstack/react-router'\n\nfunction SearchControls() {\n  const navigate = useNavigate()\n\n  const handleSortChange = (sortBy: string) => {\n    navigate({\n      search: (prev) => ({ ...prev, sort: sortBy, page: 1 }),\n    })\n  }\n\n  const handleClearFilters = () => {\n    navigate({\n      search: (prev) => {\n        const { category, minPrice, maxPrice, ...rest } = prev\n        return rest\n      },\n    })\n  }\n\n  const handleSearch = (query: string) => {\n    navigate({\n      to: '/search',\n      search: { query, page: 1 },\n    })\n  }\n\n  return (\n    <div>\n      <select onChange={(e) => handleSortChange(e.target.value)}>\n        <option value=\"relevance\">Sort by Relevance</option>\n        <option value=\"price-asc\">Price: Low to High</option>\n        <option value=\"price-desc\">Price: High to Low</option>\n      </select>\n\n      <button onClick={handleClearFilters}>Clear Filters</button>\n\n      <button onClick={() => handleSearch('latest products')}>\n        Search Latest\n      </button>\n    </div>\n  )\n}\n```\n\n#### Navigation with Router Instance\n\nUse the router directly only in non-React contexts where `useNavigate` or `Link` aren't available:\n\n```tsx\nimport { router } from './router' // Your router instance\n\n// ✅ Appropriate use case: Utility function outside React components\nexport function navigateFromUtility(searchParams: Record<string, any>) {\n  router.navigate({\n    search: (prev) => ({ ...prev, ...searchParams }),\n  })\n}\n\n// ✅ Appropriate use case: Event handlers in non-React code\nclass ApiService {\n  onAuthError() {\n    // Navigate to login when auth fails\n    router.navigate({\n      to: '/login',\n      search: { redirect: window.location.pathname },\n    })\n  }\n}\n\n// ✅ Appropriate use case: Global error handler\nwindow.addEventListener('unhandledrejection', (event) => {\n  if (event.reason.status === 401) {\n    router.navigate({\n      to: '/login',\n      search: { error: 'session-expired' },\n    })\n  }\n})\n```\n\n**⚠️ In React components, prefer `useNavigate` instead:**\n\n```tsx\n// ❌ Avoid in React components\nfunction Component() {\n  const router = useRouter()\n\n  const handleClick = () => {\n    router.navigate({ search: { filter: 'active' } })\n  }\n\n  return <button onClick={handleClick}>Filter</button>\n}\n\n// ✅ Use useNavigate in React components\nfunction Component() {\n  const navigate = useNavigate()\n\n  const handleClick = () => {\n    navigate({ search: { filter: 'active' } })\n  }\n\n  return <button onClick={handleClick}>Filter</button>\n}\n```\n\n## Advanced Navigation Patterns\n\n### Conditional Navigation\n\nNavigate automatically when certain conditions are met:\n\n```tsx\nimport { useEffect } from 'react'\nimport { useNavigate, useSearch } from '@tanstack/react-router'\n\nfunction ConditionalNavigation() {\n  const navigate = useNavigate()\n  const search = useSearch({ from: '/products' })\n\n  // Auto-reset page when search query changes\n  useEffect(() => {\n    if (search.query && search.page > 1) {\n      navigate({\n        search: (prev) => ({ ...prev, page: 1 }),\n      })\n    }\n  }, [search.query, search.page, navigate])\n\n  return <div>Page resets automatically when search changes</div>\n}\n```\n\n## Common Patterns\n\n## Common Problems\n\n### Search Parameters Not Updating\n\n**Problem:** Link navigation doesn't update search parameters.\n\n```tsx\n// ❌ Wrong - no search prop\n<Link to=\"/products\">Electronics</Link>\n\n// ✅ Correct - with search parameters\n<Link to=\"/products\" search={{ category: 'electronics' }}>\n  Electronics\n</Link>\n```\n\n### Losing Existing Search Parameters\n\n**Problem:** New navigation replaces all search parameters instead of updating specific ones.\n\n```tsx\n// ❌ Wrong - replaces all search params\n<Link search={{ page: 2 }}>Next Page</Link>\n\n// ✅ Correct - preserves existing search params\n<Link search={(prev) => ({ ...prev, page: 2 })}>\n  Next Page\n</Link>\n```\n\n## Common Next Steps\n\nAfter mastering navigation with search parameters, you might want to:\n\n- [Validate Search Parameters with Schemas](./validate-search-params.md) - Add robust validation with Zod, Valibot, or ArkType\n- [Work with Arrays, Objects, and Dates](./arrays-objects-dates-search-params.md) - Handle arrays, objects, dates, and nested data structures\n\n<!-- Uncomment when guides are available\n- [Share Search Parameters Across Routes](./share-search-params-across-routes.md) - Inherit and manage search params across route hierarchies\n-->\n\n## Related Resources\n\n- [TanStack Router Search Params Guide](https://tanstack.com/router/latest/docs/framework/react/guide/search-params) - Official documentation\n"}
